    "questionNumber": 28,
    "stem": "Bob Liodice holds that setting DNT as a default _______.",
    "stemTranslation": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "goes against human nature.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONCEPT_DISTORTION",
        "analysis": "偷换概念与张冠李戴。第五段 S12 提到‘Human nature being what it is, most people stick with default settings’，意为人性的弱点就是习惯于沿用默认设置，因此如果默认关闭追踪大家就不会去改；这说明‘沿用默认设置符合人性惰性’，而绝非‘将DNT设为默认违背了人性’。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "number",
            "ipa": "[ˈnʌmbə(r)]",
            "meaning": "…的数量",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "fails to affect the ad industry.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONTRADICTION",
        "analysis": "正反混淆。本段首句即强调‘Advertisers are horrified’，全段都在表达如果默认开启DNT将给广告业带来严重冲击，绝非‘无法影响广告行业’。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "fails",
            "ipa": "",
            "meaning": "未能",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          },
          {
            "word": "affect",
            "ipa": "[əˈfekt]",
            "meaning": "影响",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "will not benefit consumers.",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "analysis": "定位至第五段 S14：“Bob Liodice ... says consumers will be worse off if the industry cannot collect information about their preferences.” Liodice 明确宣称：如果广告业不能收集用户偏好信息，消费者的处境只会更糟（worse off），他们不会少看广告，反而会充斥着无针对性的垃圾骚扰信息。这表明他认为将DNT设为默认不仅不会给消费者带来好处，反而对消费者有害无益（will not benefit consumers）。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "benefit",
            "ipa": "[ˈbenɪfɪt]",
            "meaning": "使受益",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "may cut the number of junk ads.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONTRADICTION",
        "analysis": "正反混淆与事实颠倒。Liodice 在第五段明确指出‘People will not get fewer ads ... They'll get less meaningful, less targeted ads’，即广告数量绝不会少，只是无意义垃圾广告增多，并非减少垃圾广告。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "goes",
            "ipa": "",
            "meaning": "违背",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          },
          {
            "word": "human",
            "ipa": "[ˈhjuːmən]",
            "meaning": "人性",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      }
    ],
    "officialAnswer": "C",
    "standardType": "DETAIL",
    "type": null,
    "targetSentences": null,
    "verbatimEvidence": null,
    "synonymMapping": {
      "will not benefit consumers": "consumers will be worse off (消费者境况反而会变得更糟 -> 对消费者无益)"
    },
    "methodologyReview": "人物观点细节题。考查核心短语 worse off 的反向理解。worse off 意为‘境况更差’，等价于 will not benefit consumers。选项 D 则是考研极其高频的‘张冠李戴/概念倒置’陷阱：原文说‘人性本质是习惯保留默认’，选项偷换为‘默认设置违背人性’。",
